From 7bf7962d54d5bc7a42e8b585274b9f9821332ca1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Heidelberg <david@ixit.cz>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 11:25:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 15322/15333] arm64: dts: qcom: sdm845-shift-axolotl: add
 wcd934x MBHC thresholds

The wcd9340 codec node is missing the MBHC voltage thresholds, so the
driver logs "missing qcom,mbhc-*-vthreshold-microvolt" and headset/
headphone/button detection falls back to defaults. Add the thresholds so
jack/button detection works.

All three values are validated against the downstream android 4.9 axolotl
sources:
  - headset: qcom,msm-mbhc-hs-mic-max-threshold-mv = <1700>  -> 1700000 uV
  - headphone: qcom,msm-mbhc-hs-mic-min-threshold-mv = <50>  -> 50000 uV
  - buttons: the sdm845 machine driver (techpack/audio/asoc/sdm845.c)
    hardcodes the default btn_high[] = 75/150/237/500/500/500/500/500 mV
    when qcom,msm-mbhc-btln-threshold-mv is absent (which it is for
    axolotl), i.e. 75000/150000/237000/500000x5 uV.

Assisted-by: tencent:hy3
Signed-off-by: David Heidelberg <david@ixit.cz>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-shift-axolotl.dts | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-shift-axolotl.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-shift-axolotl.dts
index 28bb33eed575..11c188cdd8f2 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-shift-axolotl.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-shift-axolotl.dts
@@ -1462,3 +1462,10 @@ &q6cvs {
 &q6mvm {
 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+&wcd9340 {
+	qcom,mbhc-buttons-vthreshold-microvolt = <75000 150000 237000 500000
+						  500000 500000 500000 500000>;
+	qcom,mbhc-headphone-vthreshold-microvolt = <50000>;
+	qcom,mbhc-headset-vthreshold-microvolt = <1700000>;
+};
-- 
2.55.0

